{"name":"Co Pilot","hex":"#4978a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"co-pilot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["UK standard spelling of copilot."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["UK standard spelling of copilot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/co-pilot"}],"entries":[{"title":"First officer (aviation)","blocks":[{"text":"In aviation, the first officer (FO), also called co-pilot, is a pilot who serves as the second-in-command of an aircraft, alongside the captain, who is the legal commander. In the event of incapacitation of the captain, the first officer will assume command of the aircraft."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Wideroe-dash8-cockpit.jpg/330px-Wideroe-dash8-cockpit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_officer_(aviation)","wikidata":"Q123030"},{"title":"Aircraft pilot","blocks":[{"text":"An aircraft pilot is an individual who controls an aircraft's flight by operating its directional controls. Other aircrew members, such as navigators and flight engineers, are also considered aviators because they assist in operating the aircraft’s navigation and engine systems. Aircrew members like drone operators, flight attendants, mechanics, and ground crew are not classified as aviators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Lt_Mike_Hunter_1.jpg/330px-Lt_Mike_Hunter_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aircraft_pilot","wikidata":"Q2095549"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Transaero_777_landing_at_Sharm-el-Sheikh_Pereslavtsev.jpg/500px-Transaero_777_landing_at_Sharm-el-Sheikh_Pereslavtsev.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Transaero_777_landing_at_S